# What never needs to reach a build context.
#
# The Docker build compiles the language from C source, so it needs `native/`,
# `selfhost/`, `tools/`, `build.sh` and whichever example is being built --
# and nothing else. Everything below is either history, a build output, or
# something that would invalidate the cache on every commit.

.git
.github
.gitattributes
.claude

# Build outputs. The image builds its own; shipping a Windows or macOS binary
# into a Linux build context would at best be ignored and at worst be used.
/funny
/funny.exe
/funnyrt
/funnyrt.exe
/hello_standalone
/hello_standalone.exe
/funny_tsan
*.o
*.obj
*.exp
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk
/build/
/bootstrap/*.funnypak
*.funnyc
*.funnypak

# Docs and plans: read by people, not by the compiler.
*.md
!README.md
docs/

# Editor and OS litter.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
